<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">One trigger that brands often skip is the failed delivery attempt. Rather than just asking “delivery failed,” a good message lets the customer fix it with </span><a href="/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><span style="font-weight: 400;">interactive buttons like quick-reply buttons</span></a><span style="font-weight: 400;">. </span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Like,</span><i><span style="font-weight: 400;"> “Hey Sia, we tried delivering your order, but no one is available for pickup. Tap “Reschedule” to pick a new time or tap “ Cancel” to confirm cancellation. </span></i></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">It turns a one-way alert into a seamless two-way conversation that helps online stores resolve customer queries instantly. </span></p>
