<div class="custom-faq-accordion" aria-label="Frequently Asked Questions"><h2 id="frequently-asked-questions">Frequently Asked Questions</h2><div class="faq-item"><button class="faq-question open" type="button" aria-expanded="true" aria-controls="faq-answer-0"><span class="faq-title"><h3 id="are-automated-whatsapp-delivery-notifications-free-to-send">Are automated WhatsApp delivery notifications free to send?</h3></span><span class="faq-arrow" aria-hidden="true"></span></button><div id="faq-answer-0" class="faq-answer open" role="region" aria-hidden="false" style="max-height:none;">No. To send automated delivery messages, businesses need to access the WhatsApp API and pay for provider fees and Meta’s conversation pricing. However, sending utility templates within a 24-hour messaging window is free.</div></div><div class="faq-item"><button class="faq-question" type="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-answer-1"><span class="faq-title"><h3 id="can-customers-reply-to-an-automated-delivery-notification">Can customers reply to an automated delivery notification?</h3></span><span class="faq-arrow" aria-hidden="true"></span></button><div id="faq-answer-1" class="faq-answer" role="region" aria-hidden="true">Yes. WhatsApp offers two-way communication that lets customers reply to delivery notifications, ask questions, request support, and share delivery instructions.</div></div><div class="faq-item"><button class="faq-question" type="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-answer-2"><span class="faq-title"><h3 id="do-ai-chatbots-handle-delivery-related-customer-questions">Do AI chatbots handle delivery-related customer questions?</h3></span><span class="faq-arrow" aria-hidden="true"></span></button><div id="faq-answer-2" class="faq-answer" role="region" aria-hidden="true">Yes. Businesses can deploy an AI chatbot to answer common customer queries or share tracking links without any human intervention. Automation platforms like HelloBotz offer a drag-and-drop AI chatbot builder to make the setup easy and reduce coding headaches.</div></div><div class="faq-item"><button class="faq-question" type="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-answer-3"><span class="faq-title"><h3 id="is-it-possible-to-automate-whatsapp-delivery-notifications-with-shopify-or-other-ecommerce-platforms">Is it possible to automate WhatsApp delivery notifications with Shopify or other eCommerce platforms?</h3></span><span class="faq-arrow" aria-hidden="true"></span></button><div id="faq-answer-3" class="faq-answer" role="region" aria-hidden="true">Yes. With an official WhatsApp API provider like HelloBotz, brands can easily integrate WhatsApp with e-commerce platforms like Shopify, WooCommerce, and others to automatically send order updates.</div></div><div class="faq-item"><button class="faq-question" type="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-answer-4"><span class="faq-title"><h3 id="what-happens-if-a-delivery-notification-template-gets-rejected">What happens if a delivery notification template gets rejected?</h3></span><span class="faq-arrow" aria-hidden="true"></span></button><div id="faq-answer-4" class="faq-answer" role="region" aria-hidden="true">In such cases, Meta generally shares a reason behind the rejection. It can be due to category mismatch or an unclear message variable. Just fix the issue and submit for approval.</div></div></div><script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"Are automated WhatsApp delivery notifications free to send?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"No. To send automated delivery messages, businesses need to access the WhatsApp API and pay for provider fees and Meta’s conversation pricing. However, sending utility templates within a 24-hour messaging window is free."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can customers reply to an automated delivery notification?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. WhatsApp offers two-way communication that lets customers reply to delivery notifications, ask questions, request support, and share delivery instructions."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Do AI chatbots handle delivery-related customer questions?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. Businesses can deploy an AI chatbot to answer common customer queries or share tracking links without any human intervention. Automation platforms like HelloBotz offer a drag-and-drop AI chatbot builder to make the setup easy and reduce coding headaches."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Is it possible to automate WhatsApp delivery notifications with Shopify or other eCommerce platforms?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. With an official WhatsApp API provider like HelloBotz, brands can easily integrate WhatsApp with e-commerce platforms like Shopify, WooCommerce, and others to automatically send order updates."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What happens if a delivery notification template gets rejected?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"In such cases, Meta generally shares a reason behind the rejection. It can be due to category mismatch or an unclear message variable. Just fix the issue and submit for approval."}}]}</script>
    <script>
    (function(){
        if (window.__customFaqAccordionInit) return;
        window.__customFaqAccordionInit = true;

        function closeAnswer(answer, btn) {
            if (!answer) return;
            // if maxHeight is "none", set to current px value to animate to 0
            if (answer.style.maxHeight === "none" || answer.style.maxHeight === "") {
                answer.style.maxHeight = answer.scrollHeight + "px";
            }
            // force reflow
            void answer.offsetHeight;
            answer.style.maxHeight = "0px";
            answer.classList.remove("open");
            if (btn) {
                btn.classList.remove("open");
                btn.setAttribute("aria-expanded", "false");
            }
            answer.setAttribute("aria-hidden", "true");
        }

        function openAnswer(answer, btn) {
            if (!answer) return;
            // set to exact height so transition works
            answer.style.maxHeight = answer.scrollHeight + "px";
            answer.classList.add("open");
            if (btn) {
                btn.classList.add("open");
                btn.setAttribute("aria-expanded", "true");
            }
            answer.setAttribute("aria-hidden", "false");

            // once transition finishes, set to none to allow internal content changes (images) without clipping
            var onTransEnd = function(e){
                if (answer.classList.contains("open")) {
                    answer.style.maxHeight = "none";
                }
                answer.removeEventListener("transitionend", onTransEnd);
            };
            answer.addEventListener("transitionend", onTransEnd);
        }

        document.addEventListener("click", function(e){
            var btn = e.target.closest ? e.target.closest(".custom-faq-accordion .faq-question") : null;
            if (!btn) return;

            var item = btn.closest(".faq-item");
            if (!item) return;
            var answer = item.querySelector(".faq-answer");
            if (!answer) return;

            // if already open, close it
            if (answer.classList.contains("open")) {
                closeAnswer(answer, btn);
            } else {
                // optionally close other open items (uncomment to allow only-one-open)
                var openItems = document.querySelectorAll(".custom-faq-accordion .faq-answer.open");
                openItems.forEach(function(o){
                    var parentBtn = o.closest(".faq-item") ? o.closest(".faq-item").querySelector(".faq-question") : null;
                    if (o !== answer) closeAnswer(o, parentBtn);
                });

                openAnswer(answer, btn);
            }
        });

        // Make sure open answers recalc height on window resize (useful if images load or layout changes)
        window.addEventListener("resize", function(){
            var openAnswers = document.querySelectorAll(".custom-faq-accordion .faq-answer.open");
            openAnswers.forEach(function(a){
                // if maxHeight is "none", set it to scrollHeight to keep it visible after resize
                if (a.style.maxHeight === "none") {
                    a.style.maxHeight = a.scrollHeight + "px";
                    // then release to none after a tick
                    setTimeout(function(){ a.style.maxHeight = "none"; }, 350);
                }
            });
        });
    })();
    </script>
    
